> The mirrors move to simulate day and night phases, no reason why they can't
> move slowly enough to give different sun positions that almost map to a
> natural day - but yes, it might be confusing that the light source starts
> and ends in the same place for both sunrise and sunset.  Wind might have to
> be artificially enhanced, as might pollination of crops - insectoid robots
> perhaps?

For pollination, we could bring a variety of bees - no reason to limit it to 
Apis mellifera, which has the waggle dance to tell fellow bees the direction 
to the flowers. Solitary bees would work just as well for pollinating, and 
may not have the polarization problem.

